								"uidString" : "FKjhUCR3THacOeSPHRL7qg=="
							},
							"paragraphStyle" : {
								"__type" : "textStyle"
							},
							"string" : "002 puts the file at the bottom of the scope stack. But a `FAMIXFile` doesn't contain declarations and doesn't know its namespace: it only knows its `parentFolder` and its `entities`. It's where the source text lives, not a scope."
						},
						{
							"__type" : "textSnippet",
							"children" : {
								"__type" : "snippets",
								"items" : [ ]
							},
							"createEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"createTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-10-25T14:26:41.126451+02:00"
								}
							},
							"editEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"editTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-10-25T14:26:41.126451+02:00"
								}
							},
							"uid" : {
								"__type" : "uid",
								"uidString" : "Ggstd5xUTl2BwhQew8OKzw=="
							},
							"paragraphStyle" : {
								"__type" : "textStyle"
							},
							"string" : "{{gtClass:GtPythonImporter}}, {{gtClass:GtJSImporter}} and {{gtClass:GtRubyImporter}} all keep a `currentFile` slot beside their `scopeStack`, read by `sourceAnchorFor:` ({{gtMethod:GtPythonImporter>>sourceAnchorFor:}}). Their scope stacks hold modules, classes and functions."
						},
						{
							"__type" : "textSnippet",
							"children" : {
								"__type" : "snippets",
								"items" : [ ]
							},
							"createEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"createTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-10-25T14:26:41.293465+02:00"
								}
							},
							"editEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"editTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-10-25T14:26:41.293465+02:00"
								}
							},
							"uid" : {
								"__type" : "uid",
								"uidString" : "+Y8h0UrMROKxTun0R9Vy/A=="
							},
							"paragraphStyle" : {
								"__type" : "textStyle"
							},
							"string" : "Supertypes are resolved after every file has been walked, when there is no current file any more. Python and JS resolve references per file (`finishImportingFile`), so they never meet this. Ruby resolves superclasses after all files and gives its inheritances no source anchor ({{gtMethod:GtRubyImporter>>assignSuperclass:to:}})."
						},
						{
							"__type" : "textSnippet",
							"children" : {
								"__type" : "snippets",
								"items" : [ ]
							},
							"createEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"createTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-10-25T14:26:41.497307+02:00"
								}
							},
							"editEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"editTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-10-25T14:26:41.497307+02:00"
								}
							},
							"uid" : {
								"__type" : "uid",
								"uidString" : "zjQljCVhQJm+hhyqGh+2HQ=="
							},
							"paragraphStyle" : {
								"__type" : "textStyle"
							},
							"string" : "The other importers do store AST attributes, but to map a node to the entity it produced, e.g. `#modelObject` in {{gtMethod:GtPythonImporter>>ensureFunctionNamed:for:around:}}, read back in {{gtMethod:GtPythonImporter>>modelObjectFrom:in:}}. 002's \"nothing reads AST attributes\" could be read as forbidding that too."
						}
					]
				},
